Z||000000||CUTTER||10-26-1999||03:41 PM||||people are telling me to drill holes in my airbox and it will give me a few extra HP. Is this true? and if so How many holes should I drill in it and what size?<BR>  Thanx, Shane||||reg||1
Z||000001||Patrick||10-26-1999||04:05 PM||||<BR>What is an "airbox"? I'm not familiar with that term. Are you referring to the can that the air filter sits in?<P>If that's what you're referring to, I'd say it's a bad idea. Drilling holes in it would allow <B>hot</B> engine compartment air to enter the intake system, when what we really want is the coldest air possible.||||reg||5
Z||000002||lowCG||10-26-1999||05:40 PM||||Really depends on the requirements of the engine,and how restrictive the existing system is.<BR>From what I've seen,and read from other's experience is that the air system is fine the way it is,and isn't the weak point in the system.<BR>My old 16V Jetta perked up when I removed a large portion of the airbox(filter housing) that looked as if it were meant to be removed by the way it was molded. <BR>And,like Patrick noted,a supply of fresh air,or an installation where there's nothing crowding around the airbox ((a good couple of inches)works well too I've found.<p>[This message has been edited by lowCG (edited 10-26-1999).]||||reg||1
